{"step_index":79,"source":"SYSTEM","type":"CHECKPOINT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-08T04:51:37Z","content":"{{ CHECKPOINT 0 }}\n **The earlier parts of this conversation have been truncated due to its long length. The following content summarizes the truncated context so that you may continue your work. **\n\n\n# User Requests\nThe following were user requests from the truncated conversation in chronological order:\n1. Develop a software supply chain security platform for managing software dependencies and build artifacts. The system should register projects, record dependencies, scan dependency versions, identify vulnerable packages, generate risk reports, and track remediations.\nStudents can model a simplified developer → source repository → build → dependencies → security scan → artifact repository workflow.\nAddress the following development security challenges: dependency confusion attacks, malicious packages, artifact tampering, build compromise, secret leakage, and supply chain attacks.\n\n\n# Previous Session Summary:\n# Session Continuation Summary\n\n## 1. Outstanding User Requests\n\n### PRIMARY REQUEST — Status: IMPLEMENTATION (in progress, ~60% complete)\n\n> **User:** \"Develop a software supply chain security platform for managing software dependencies and build artifacts. The system should register projects, record dependencies, scan dependency versions, identify vulnerable packages, generate risk reports, and track remediations. Students can model a simplified developer → source repository → build → dependencies → security scan → artifact repository workflow. Address the following development security challenges: dependency confusion attacks, malicious packages, artifact tampering, build compromise, secret leakage, and supply chain attacks.\"\n\nThe platform is named **SecureChain**. Backend is ~95% complete. Frontend is ~50% complete — several pages still need to be written, npm packages installed, and the whole system needs to be run/ve